WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.005 --> 00:00:04.742
book "Untouchable: How powerful

00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:08.679
people get away with it"

00:00:08.679 --> 00:00:10.114
rocketing up the charts right

00:00:10.248 --> 00:00:10.681
now.

00:00:10.681 --> 00:00:16.287
What report do we have about

00:00:16.687 --> 00:00:17.688
what's going on?

00:00:17.822 --> 00:00:18.222
&gt;&gt; There are three

00:00:18.356 --> 00:00:18.956
investigations swirling around

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:19.390
Donald Trump.

00:00:19.523 --> 00:00:20.091
We have been here before, the

00:00:20.224 --> 00:00:20.691
swirling phase.

00:00:20.691 --> 00:00:21.292
Number of them have resulted in

00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:21.692
indictment.

00:00:21.826 --> 00:00:22.693
Let's take stock starting with

00:00:22.693 --> 00:00:24.028
that justice department

00:00:24.161 --> 00:00:24.996
investigation.

00:00:25.129 --> 00:00:28.699
It has -- it was 73 days ago, I

00:00:28.699 --> 00:00:29.967
counted, when Merrick Garland

00:00:30.101 --> 00:00:31.202
appointed jack Smith as special

00:00:31.335 --> 00:00:31.535
counsel.

00:00:31.669 --> 00:00:33.904
Jack Smith has two jobs, to

00:00:34.038 --> 00:00:37.341
investigate January 6th first of

00:00:37.475 --> 00:00:37.608
all.

00:00:37.742 --> 00:00:39.944
We have not seen movement on

00:00:40.077 --> 00:00:40.244
that.

00:00:40.378 --> 00:00:40.978
Could be happening behind closed

00:00:41.112 --> 00:00:43.014
doors and to investigate the

00:00:43.147 --> 00:00:43.714
mar-a-lago documents scandal.

00:00:43.848 --> 00:00:48.252
As you said, we have reporting

00:00:48.386 --> 00:00:50.087
that two people have gone into

00:00:50.221 --> 00:00:51.155
the grand jury that recovered

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:51.622
those documents.

00:00:51.756 --> 00:00:53.090
That tells us that jack Smith

00:00:53.224 --> 00:00:54.225
continues to move ahead in that

00:00:54.358 --> 00:00:55.493
part of the investigation.

00:00:55.626 --> 00:00:56.727
Now how is this going to play

00:00:56.727 --> 00:00:57.395
for now?

00:00:57.528 --> 00:00:58.729
When jack Smith is ready, he

00:00:58.729 --> 00:01:00.298
will make a recommendation to

00:01:00.731 --> 00:01:01.799
the attorney general, indict or

00:01:01.932 --> 00:01:02.366
don't indict.

00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:04.802
The final word, however, is up

00:01:04.935 --> 00:01:05.336
to Merrick Garland.

00:01:05.469 --> 00:01:06.737
By law, he has to give jack

00:01:06.804 --> 00:01:08.005
Smith's recommendations, quote,

00:01:08.139 --> 00:01:08.739
great weight.

00:01:08.806 --> 00:01:12.743
So we'll see how this plays out.

00:01:12.843 --> 00:01:13.411
Ultimately this will be up to

00:01:13.544 --> 00:01:13.878
Merrick Garland.

00:01:14.011 --> 00:01:15.513
&gt;&gt; Of course, Bonnie Willis in

00:01:15.646 --> 00:01:16.881
Georgia is looking into former

00:01:17.014 --> 00:01:17.815
president trump's alleged

00:01:17.948 --> 00:01:19.050
efforts to overturn the election

00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:21.786
in that state.

00:01:21.919 --> 00:01:23.654
How could that affect the 2024

00:01:23.788 --> 00:01:24.755
presidential campaign?

00:01:24.755 --> 00:01:25.589
&gt;&gt; This could be the most

00:01:25.723 --> 00:01:27.058
immediate case of all the

00:01:27.191 --> 00:01:28.292
pending cases.

00:01:28.426 --> 00:01:29.060
The district attorney we found

00:01:29.193 --> 00:01:29.894
out in the last couple of weeks

00:01:30.027 --> 00:01:31.996
has finished her presentation to

00:01:32.129 --> 00:01:33.531
the special grand jury.

00:01:33.664 --> 00:01:34.765
We're not seeing that report as

00:01:34.765 --> 00:01:35.366
of this moment.

00:01:35.499 --> 00:01:37.168
The special grand jury cannot

00:01:37.301 --> 00:01:38.202
indict, but what the special

00:01:38.336 --> 00:01:40.004
grand jury can do is make a

00:01:40.137 --> 00:01:40.771
recommendation.

00:01:40.871 --> 00:01:42.773
Ultimately, again, it will be up

00:01:42.807 --> 00:01:43.574
to Bonnie Willis whether she

00:01:43.708 --> 00:01:47.812
wants to go to a regular jury,

00:01:47.945 --> 00:01:50.281
to seek an indictment, and fan

00:01:50.414 --> 00:01:52.216
Willis said to a judge, that,

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.751
quote, decisions are iminnocent.

00:01:53.884 --> 00:01:55.920
Now people asked me mean, is

00:01:56.053 --> 00:01:57.221
that a legal technical word?

00:01:57.355 --> 00:01:57.488
No.

00:01:57.621 --> 00:01:58.923
It means imminent.

00:01:59.056 --> 00:01:59.757
It means soon.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.926
Whatever fani Willis thinks is

00:02:02.059 --> 00:02:04.795
soon, is soon, but I would take

00:02:04.795 --> 00:02:05.296
her at her word and I think we

00:02:05.429 --> 00:02:07.331
will hear what her decisions

00:02:07.465 --> 00:02:07.598
are.

00:02:07.732 --> 00:02:10.267
&gt;&gt; How about that hush money

00:02:10.401 --> 00:02:13.204
payment to stormy Daniels?

00:02:13.337 --> 00:02:13.738
Is that back again?

00:02:13.871 --> 00:02:14.438
&gt;&gt; This is the oldest and the

00:02:14.805 --> 00:02:14.905
newest.

00:02:14.905 --> 00:02:16.407
This dates back to 2016, but

00:02:16.807 --> 00:02:17.241
there are brand-new developments

00:02:17.375 --> 00:02:17.541
here.

00:02:17.675 --> 00:02:18.809
We've just learned that the new

00:02:18.809 --> 00:02:21.345
York D.A., the Manhattan D.A., a

00:02:21.479 --> 00:02:22.880
state-level prosecutor here in

00:02:23.013 --> 00:02:23.981
Manhattan is going to put

00:02:24.115 --> 00:02:25.516
evidence of these hush money

00:02:25.649 --> 00:02:27.284
payments in front of a grand

00:02:27.418 --> 00:02:27.585
jury.

00:02:27.718 --> 00:02:29.553
That could result in an

00:02:29.687 --> 00:02:30.421
indictment, and it's interesting

00:02:30.821 --> 00:02:32.823
because this goes back so far in

00:02:32.857 --> 00:02:34.225
time, and I think the question

00:02:34.358 --> 00:02:35.292
is what has happened?

00:02:35.426 --> 00:02:39.597
This goes back 6 1/2 years to

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:40.865
before the campaign.

